+The prior candidate (local `f293afbc45de24d15614e8c804844de0d6e01d12`, tree `c2f7c88ac2d02ce631b77bc7b53eee1f9901eff8`) and its archive/patch/evidence hashes matched. All 26 newly supplied package hashes matched the supplied checksum manifest. The restored existing offline GUI pool combined with the individual package inputs contains 470 packages after duplicate elimination. APT simulation and actual offline install on Debian 13 systemd/cgroup-v2 guest exit 0; all seven required desktop packages installed, no dpkg audit output. APT used a local repository constructed from the retained checksum-checked package archives; no new signed Debian index verification was performed in this run. No NIC, only loopback. Exact 293 parent tracked file hashes matched after unpacking the archive. Parent had no installed portfolio; independently provisioned controlled synthetic PAPER fixture only.
+
+## Repairs and deployment
+
+The initial installed provisioning correctly refused group-writable archive modes; installed directory and code permissions tightened without changing bytes. Real LightDM authenticated the test approval identity but the default Debian Xsession wrapper misparsed the quoted Python `-c` desktop command and automatically added an X11 local-user access grant, incompatible with the strict no-extra-grants contract. Replace that entry with a fixed root-owned executable wrapper; on a reviewed dedicated LightDM seat use the same executable as `session-wrapper`. It only accepts the exact single fixed session executable argument, executes the isolated Python session, and does not invoke general Xsession hooks, permit arbitrary commands, grant X11 access, change authorization deadlines or enable auto-login. `deploy/90-maj-vaj-approval-lightdm.conf.example` records the dedicated-seat settings actually used; do not apply to a shared workstation. The provisioning script checks the wrapper's ownership/mode/executability, refuses differing configuration; administrator explicitly reconciles old desktop entry and reviews seat configuration. The production unit, cookie/session guards, independent signing, and financial gates remain unchanged. New wrapper tests 2/2; full focused review suite 17/17 under Xvfb. An initial focused run without a display failed the GUI test; repeated in a real host test display and passed. Full repository suite not rerun; prior 506/508 (two skips) is retained for the parent only.
+
+## Installed acceptance
+
+Actual offline QEMU standard VGA virtual console, genuine LightDM/PAM login via console keyboard using separate disposable test login credential. Initial invalid login correctly refused; next correct login authenticated but old launch entry failed as described. Corrected fixed wrapper deployed byte-for-byte, genuine login again, actual logind active local unlocked X11 seat0 user session and strict X11 ACL; private copied approval cookie mode 0600. Ordinary desk UID cannot attach and cannot start named review unit via polkit. Real production launcher visibly starts the actual named protected graphical review service (no review ExecStart override); actual UI inputs via virtual console, synthetic passphrase only. Native and proof services use the already established root-owned controlled-book/pre-effect interruption fixture overrides; actual Gate and ledger, signatures, proof producer, desk importer and archival roles remain independent. First invalid UI submission refused, no pending approval/financial release; close and reopen; valid input produces independently signed approval. Two consecutive cycles on same portfolio, keys and mailboxes, each held $27.55 reservation until verified recovery. Exact independent archive copies authenticated, duplicates imported without new ledger effects, two reviewed NO_FILL events, zero native orders, zero reservations/P&L, $100 principal unchanged and both pause flags set. Each audit exit 0. Both native and authority pending records retired. Production display session exit via launcher retired cookie; post-logout polkit start denied and service MainPID zero. Test services/timers stopped, fixture overrides removed, opt-in removed and synthetic login locked. Actual disk shutdown clean; qemu-img check zero errors; original Debian base SHA256 `2eba10bdfc7f368dde145205e0f3211f5f3a0ce29a5ab60b5ea7b728fd9a1776` unchanged. No physical workstation tested, no real market, no profitability claim.
+
+## Remaining gates
+
+Independently qualify actual in-window cancel (before submission) and lock/seat-switch/logoff-before-confirm refusal under real installed approval seat; post-logout refusal and previous focused guards pass. Proceed to TB-SEC-KEY-01, sustained public PAPER with genuine networked constructor, migrated financial-goal acceptance, TB-12 forward validation and final consolidated acceptance. No LIVE authority.
